<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>SIG model brief {{ as_of }}</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; max-width: 860px;
         margin: 32px auto; padding: 0 20px; color: #1f2328; line-height: 1.45; }
  h1 { font-size: 24px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
  h2 { font-size: 17px; margin-top: 32px; border-bottom: 1px solid #d0d7de; padding-bottom: 4px; }
  .meta { color: #59636e; font-size: 13px; }
  .mode { display: inline-block; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 6px; font-weight: 600;
          background: #ddf4ff; color: #0550ae; margin: 10px 0; }
  .mode.rb { background: #fff8c5; color: #7d4e00; }
  .demo { background: #ffebe9; color: #82071e; padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 14px; }
  .lead { font-size: 15px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 13px; margin: 8px 0; }
  th, td { padding: 4px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eaeef2; text-align: right; }
  th:first-child, td:first-child { text-align: left; }
  thead th { background: #f6f8fa; }
  img { max-width: 100%; }
  .note { color: #59636e; font-size: 12.5px; }
  .ok { color: #1a7f37; } .bad { color: #cf222e; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>SIG model brief: {{ as_of }}</h1>
<div class="meta">Returns through {{ returns_through }} · macro data as published by {{ as_of }} · portfolio ${{ aum }}</div>

{% if demo_views %}
<p class="demo"><strong>Demo views.</strong> No analyst view sheet was found, so this brief uses the
fictional views in <code>views/view_sheet_demo.csv</code>. They are illustrations, not research.</p>
{% endif %}

<div class="mode {{ 'rb' if mode == 'risk_budget' else '' }}">Engine mode: {{ mode_label }}</div>
<p class="lead">{{ headline }}</p>

<h2>1. Proposed weights</h2>
<img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ chart_active }}" alt="Active weights">
{{ weights_table | safe }}
<p class="note">$ columns are the position vs benchmark on a ${{ aum }} portfolio.</p>

<h2>2. Macro state</h2>
<p>{{ regime_sentence }}</p>
{{ regime_table | safe }}
<p>{{ recession_sentence }}</p>
<img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ chart_recession }}" alt="Recession probability">
<p class="note">{{ recession_scores }}</p>
<p><strong>Scenario priors for the analysts' matrix:</strong></p>
{{ scenario_table | safe }}
<p><strong>Analog check (months whose economy looked most like today):</strong> average next-12-month
relative return, annualized %. Use as a sanity check on views, not as a signal.</p>
{{ analog_table | safe }}

<h2>3. Evidence: signal scorecard (frozen by <code>make research</code>)</h2>
<p>{{ scorecard_sentence }}</p>
{{ scorecard_table | safe }}
<p class="note">A signal needs a positive mean IC with Holm-adjusted p &lt; 0.05 for "oos_value" (confidence 4),
or t ≥ 1 for "weak" (confidence 2). The power threshold is the smallest IC this sample could reliably detect.</p>

<h2>4. Views and what they did</h2>
{% if views_table %}
{{ views_table | safe }}
{% else %}<p>No views.</p>{% endif %}
{% if attribution_table %}
<p><strong>Leave-one-view-out:</strong> how much each view moved the portfolio.</p>
{{ attribution_table | safe }}
{% endif %}

<h2>5. Risk</h2>
{{ risk_table | safe }}
<img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ chart_contrib }}" alt="Tracking-error contributions">
<p><strong>Policy checks:</strong>
{% for k, v in checks.items() %}<span class="{{ 'ok' if v else 'bad' }}">{{ '✓' if v else '✗' }} {{ k }}</span>{{ " · " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</p>
<p><strong>Historical replays</strong> (today's weights through past episodes):</p>
{{ stress_table | safe }}
<p><strong>Factor shocks</strong> (through sector betas):</p>
{{ shock_table | safe }}

{% if backtest_table %}
<h2>6. Backtest of the systematic engines</h2>
<img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ chart_backtest }}" alt="Backtest">
{{ backtest_table | safe }}
<p class="note">Analyst views cannot be backtested; only the systematic engines are tested here.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Limitations to say out loud</h2>
<ul class="note">
  <li>Macro data use publication-lag rules, not ALFRED vintages, so revisions are not modelled.</li>
  <li>Benchmark weights are held at their 2026 values; sector history before an ETF existed uses proxies (IYR, SPY).</li>
  <li>Revision and valuation signals need Bloomberg exports and are skipped without them.</li>
  <li>Four US recessions since 1985 is a small sample for any recession model.</li>
</ul>
</body>
</html>
